gQf(){return"The tram crosses the road outside the intersection, not from the depot. Should I give way?"},
gQe(){return"Yes. Outside the intersection, the tram has priority except for leaving the depot (clause 18.1)."},
gQh(){return"The tram leaves the depot. Should it give way to cars?"},
gQg(){return"Yes. When leaving the depot, the tram gives way to other vehicles (clause 18.1)."},
gQj(){return"Without a traffic light at an equivalent intersection, do you need to give way to the car on the right?"},
gQi(){return"Yes. At an uncontrolled intersection of equal significance, give way to cars on the right (clause 13.11)."},
gQl(){return"Is it possible to overtake at an equivalent intersection without a traffic light?"},
gQk(){return"No. At an uncontrolled intersection, overtaking is allowed only when driving on the main road (clause 11.4)."},
gQn(){return"Is there a roundabout ahead?"},
gQm(){return"Yes. A sign warns you when approaching a roundabout."},
gQp(){return"Does the roundabout start right at this sign?"},
gQo(){return"No. This is a warning. The direction of movement on the circle itself is set by sign 4.3."},
gPQ(){return"Is it possible to turn around if the road is only visible at 70 m?"},
gPP(){return"No. To turn around, visibility must be at least 100 m in each direction (clause 8.11)."},
gPS(){return"Before a dangerous turn, should you choose a safe speed?"},
gPR(){return"Yes. The speed is chosen taking into account the turn and visibility of the road (clause 10.1)."},
gQ_(){return"Could children suddenly come onto the road here?"},
gPZ(){return"Yes. The sign warns of an area where children may appear on the road."},
gQ1(){return"Does this sign allow children to cross the road anywhere?"},
gQ0(){return"No. The sign warns drivers, but does not change the rules for crossing the road."},
gQ3(){return"A temporary sign on a yellow background is more important than a permanent one if they conflict?"},
gQ2(){return"Yes. If there is a contradiction between temporary and permanent signs, the temporary requirement is fulfilled."},
gQ5(){return"Do you have to stop at a road works sign?"},
gQ4(){return"No. The sign itself does not require stopping. You need to take roadworks into account and choose a safe speed."},
gQr(){return"Without a traffic light, do you have the right of way over a car with a second priority?"},
gQq(){return"Yes. At an uncontrolled intersection, the main road gives priority over the secondary one (clause 13.9)."},
gQt(){return"Is it possible to drive on a red light if you are on the main road?"},
gQs(){return"No. At a signalized intersection, you must follow the traffic lights (clause 6.15)."},
gQv(){return"Is it possible to park a car on the roadway of a main road outside a populated area?"},
